# This file exists so npm packaging of `.goodvibes/` is decided only by the
# "files" allowlist in package.json (.goodvibes/GOODVIBES.md, .goodvibes/agents,
# .goodvibes/skills) and never by whatever scratch-state ignore file happens to
# sit in this directory on a developer's machine.
#
# Background: running the TUI writes transient state here (logs, cache, overflow
# buffers, exec output, sessions), and tooling commonly drops a local
# `.goodvibes/.gitignore` containing `*`. npm reads ignore files per directory;
# npm 11 let an explicit package.json "files" entry win over that rule, npm 12
# does not, so on a machine with that local file npm 12 silently packed a
# tarball with no .goodvibes/GOODVIBES.md, .goodvibes/agents or
# .goodvibes/skills. `.npmignore` takes precedence over `.gitignore` in the same
# directory, so this (deliberately empty of rules) file restores identical,
# machine-independent packing on npm 11 and npm 12 alike.
#
# Do not add rules here, and do not delete this file.
